{
  "aspect": "9x16",
  "frame": {
    "w": 1080,
    "h": 1920
  },
  "format": "earnings",
  "notes": [
    "EARNINGS, on the v2 plate kit. The print against what was expected, what",
    "moved, and what it means \u2014 in the vertical set only.",
    "",
    "There is no stamp. A verdict card is a CALL, and the register is",
    "anti-Cramer by construction: he describes and the viewer decides. What",
    "was a stamp is the closing plate's own line now.",
    "",
    "A STATIC PLATE MAY HOLD. The ceiling was written when every plate in the kit boiled; 44 of the 140 are `playback: static` now, because a figure that moves is a figure being re-read. What keeps a data beat short is the ceiling itself, and it is set to what a seventy-second cut of ten beats actually gives each one."
  ],
  "shots": [
    {
      "id": "open",
      "plate": "shorts/hook-card-t2",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "hook",
      "captions": false,
      "bind": {
        "hook": "script.hook_text",
        "sub": "?script.move_summary",
        "ticker": "script.ticker"
      },
      "notes": "The hook card, second treatment \u2014 earnings is not the daily short and should not open on the same picture."
    },
    {
      "id": "the-print",
      "plate": "figures/big-number-l1-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "reported",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?numbers.headline_kicker",
        "value": "compare.reported",
        "label": "?numbers.headline_label",
        "caption": "?script.move_summary"
      },
      "notes": "The number that printed, at the size it deserves."
    },
    {
      "id": "vs-expected",
      "plate": "figures/compare-stacked-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "expected",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?compare.kicker",
        "label-1": "?numbers.headline_label",
        "value-1": "compare.reported",
        "label-2": "?compare.expected_label",
        "value-2": "?compare.expected",
        "caption": "?script.cheap_or_trap"
      },
      "notes": "Print against consensus, stacked. The delta slot holds eight characters and takes the gap."
    },
    {
      "id": "the-sheet",
      "plate": "tables/numbers-sheet-4r-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "numbers",
      "lit": "all",
      "bind": {
        "unit": "?numbers.unit",
        "head": "numbers.years",
        "label-1": "numbers.label.0",
        "row-1": "numbers.figures.0",
        "label-2": "?numbers.label.1",
        "row-2": "?numbers.figures.1",
        "label-3": "?numbers.label.2",
        "row-3": "?numbers.figures.2",
        "label-4": "?numbers.label.3",
        "row-4": "?numbers.figures.3"
      },
      "notes": "Every row up at once \u2014 an earnings cut has no time for a walk down them."
    },
    {
      "id": "guidance",
      "plate": "cards/definition-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "guidance",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?compare.kicker",
        "term": "?numbers.headline_label",
        "body": "script.guidance"
      },
      "notes": "What they said about next year, in the card drawn for a term and its meaning."
    },
    {
      "id": "the-turn",
      "plate": "room/talk",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "turn",
      "host": {
        "pose": "host/close-up",
        "slot": "host-anchor"
      },
      "notes": "The line the print actually means, told to camera in close-up."
    },
    {
      "id": "so-what",
      "plate": "structure/both-true-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "cheap_or_trap",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?compare.kicker",
        "statement-1": "compare.heavy",
        "statement-2": "compare.light",
        "caption": "?script.cheap_or_trap"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "close",
      "plate": "structure/closing-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?script.ticker",
        "line-1": "script.conclusion",
        "date-label": "?channel.handle"
      }
    }
  ]
}
